        "description": "\\# Software Engineer II, Frontend\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n \\#\\# About the Role\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Greenlight is a family technology company focused on helping families raise financially smart kids and navigate life together. Its connected products—including the Greenlight app, debit card, Safe Family GPS trackers, and Family Hub—bring financial tools, safety features, and everyday family management into one experience used by more than 6\\.5 million family members.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Greenlight is seeking a Software Engineer II, Frontend with a background in web development to join the Web Platform and Family Hub team. The role focuses on Next.js web application development, application design, and building high\\-quality web experiences while also participating in deployment and operational phases of the software development lifecycle (SDLC). The position reports to the Director, Engineering.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n \\#\\# Key Responsibilities\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n \\- Lead the design and implementation of web experiences that translate mobile features to the web with a world\\-class user experience.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Drive technical strategy for the web platform.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Define engineering standards and development best practices.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Establish the technical vision for the web platform.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Mentor engineers and contribute technical leadership.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Manage technical debt and champion code quality.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Lead architectural evolution of the web platform.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Participate in deployment and operational phases of the SDLC.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n \\#\\# Required Qualifications\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n \\- BS in Computer Science or equivalent.\n \n\n\n\n \\- 3\\+ years of software development experience.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Track record of technical leadership.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Expertise in React and Next.js or Remix.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Experience with modern build tools.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Experience with software testing.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Experience with CI/CD.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Background in web development and web application development.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Understanding of application design and development.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n \\#\\# Preferred Qualifications\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n The source job description does not specify additional preferred or nice\\-to\\-have qualifications.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n \\#\\# Skills \\& Competencies\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n \\- Frontend software development.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Web application development.\n \n\n\n\n \\- React.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Next.js.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Remix.\n \n\n\n\n \\- TypeScript.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Tailwind CSS.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Modern build tools, including Turborepo.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Software testing, including Cypress, React Testing Library, and Jest.\n \n\n\n\n \\- CI/CD.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Technical strategy and architectural design.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Engineering standards and best practices.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Code quality and technical debt management.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Technical leadership and mentoring.\n \n\n\n\n \\- User experience (UX).\n \n\n\n\n \\- Deployment and operational practices.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n \\#\\# Education \\& Experience\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n \\*\\*Education\\*\\*\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n \\- BS in Computer Science or equivalent.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n \\*\\*Experience\\*\\*\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n \\- 3\\+ years of software development experience.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Track record of technical leadership.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Expertise in React/Next.js/Remix.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Experience with modern build tools, testing, and CI/CD.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n \\#\\# Work Arrangement \\& Schedule\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n \\- \\*\\*Work arrangement:\\*\\* Remote, with flexible work\\-from\\-home and in\\-office opportunities.\n \n\n\n\n \\- \\*\\*Job location:\\*\\* Victorville, CA, US (Remote).\n \n\n\n\n \\- \\*\\*Employment type:\\*\\* Not specified in the source job description.\n \n\n\n\n \\- \\*\\*Expected weekly hours:\\*\\* Not specified.\n \n\n\n\n \\- \\*\\*Schedule flexibility:\\*\\* Flexible WFH is offered; specific working hours are not specified.\n \n\n\n\n \\- \\*\\*Weekend requirements:\\*\\* Not specified.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n \\#\\# Compensation \\& Benefits\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n \\- \\*\\*Estimated base pay range — NY, CA, WA:\\*\\* $122,000–$170,000\\.\n \n\n\n\n \\- \\*\\*Estimated base pay range — CO:\\*\\* $122,000–$145,000\\.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Competitive compensation based on location, experience, and skill set.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Discretionary performance bonus.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Equity rewards.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Medical, dental, vision, and HSA match.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Paid life insurance, AD\\&D, and disability benefits.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Traditional 401(k) with company match.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Unlimited PTO.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Paid company holidays and pop\\-up bonus holidays.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Professional development stipends.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Mental health resources.\n \n\n\n\n \\- 1:1 financial planners.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Fertility healthcare.\n \n\n\n\n \\- 100% paid parental and caregiving leave, plus cleaning service and meals during leave.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Flexible WFH and in\\-office opportunities.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Fully stocked kitchen, catered lunches, and occasional in\\-office happy hours.\n \n\n\n\n \\- Employee resource groups.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n \\#\\# Compliance / Additional Information\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Greenlight is an equal opportunity employer and will not discriminate against any employee or applicant based on age, race, color, national origin, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, religion, physical or mental disability, medical condition (including pregnancy, childbirth, or a medical condition related to pregnancy or childbirth), genetic information, marital status, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Greenlight is committed 